IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `saz-seat`

-- Cases for the seat layer (saz-seat.l4): a soldier serving within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence.
-- Expected values are written from SG § 30c, SAZV § 1 and its Anlage as deposited, not from this encoding's output.
-- Case A is the captain in the article's Case 3 "Potential exploit": posted to Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command in Germany,
-- still within the Ministry's remit, doing ordinary staff duties outside § 30c(4), ten hours of ordered overtime in one month, no compelling service reasons.
-- Arguments, in order: remit, establishment, assigned for international tasks, activity under § 30c(4), overtime hours, blocked hours (and, where asked, an exception applies).

§ `Case A: the captain at JSEC`

-- On the annex as printed, § 1(2) SAZV takes him out of § 30c(1) to (3) SG.
#ASSERT NOT (`do the working time rules apply to me under the annex as printed` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0)
#ASSERT `how many hours of time off must I be given under the annex as printed` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0 EQUALS 0
-- If the 2025 listing is void and no exception is accepted, § 30c(2) gives him time off for all ten hours.
#ASSERT `do the working time rules apply to me if the 2025 listing is void` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0 FALSE
#ASSERT `how many hours of time off must I be given if the 2025 listing is void` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0 FALSE EQUALS 10
-- If an exception to the citation requirement is accepted, the listing stands and he gets none.
#ASSERT `how many hours of time off must I be given if the 2025 listing is void` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0 TRUE EQUALS 0
-- The fact the whole case turns on: the preamble does not cite § 30c(6) with § 93(2) no. 7.
#ASSERT NOT (`does the 2025 preamble cite the power to exempt`)

§ `Case B: a soldier at SHAPE, which was already in the annex`

-- The article's argument does not touch it: no time off under either reading.
#ASSERT `how many hours of time off must I be given under the annex as printed` TRUE "Supreme Headquarters Allied Powers Europe" TRUE FALSE 10 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `how many hours of time off must I be given if the 2025 listing is void` TRUE "Supreme Headquarters Allied Powers Europe" TRUE FALSE 10 0 FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `Case C: a soldier in an ordinary German unit, six hours of overtime`

#ASSERT `do the working time rules apply to me under the annex as printed` TRUE "" FALSE FALSE 6 0
#ASSERT `how many hours of time off must I be given under the annex as printed` TRUE "" FALSE FALSE 6 0 EQUALS 6

§ `Case D: the deadline`

#ASSERT `within how many months must the time off be given` FALSE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `within how many months must the time off be given` TRUE EQUALS 6
